            0.857
          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.894,
            0.12,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": "188"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.884,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "food, and they grow. They also respire, reproduce, excrete, respond to stimuli, and eventually, die. Absence of any of these features indicates that they are **non-living** things."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.145,
            0.883,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": "Now that you know how to identify a living being, fill up the remaining two columns (IV and V) of Table 10.1 and complete the activity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.207,
            0.883,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "In which category would you place a seed—living or non-living? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.247,
            0.883,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "Let us **explore** how a seed germinates to observe some of these essential characteristics in plants."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.306,
            0.81,
            0.357
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "10.2 Essential Conditions for Germination of a Seed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.368,
            0.885,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "Have you observed a seed germinating? You might have wondered what conditions are required for **germination** of a seed. What conditions do you think are required for seed germination? How will you investigate whether these conditions have an effect on the germination of a seed? Let us find out by performing Activity 10.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.503,
            0.605,
            0.525
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 10.2: Let us experiment"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.535,
            0.883,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "Take four identical pots filled with garden soil. Sow four bean seeds in each pot. Now, keep these pots in the following conditions for 15 days."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.604,
            0.883,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "Pot A: Do not water the soil. Place this pot in direct sunlight."
        },
